//
// Inter-service gRPC contract for the Identity supporting domain
// (chora_identity database, Team 3 / Platform). REST surfaces in
// chora-contracts/openapi/identity*.yaml are the user-facing equivalents;
// gRPC is for internal service-to-service sync calls only (mTLS via
// the service mesh per CLAUDE.md §4 protocol strategy).
//
// Aggregates exposed:
//   - GlobalChoraID (GCID)        — opaque UUIDv7, cross-tenant portable
//   - PerCourseRoleContext        — projection of TenantMembership + role
//   - AccountLifecycle (saga)     — federated closure saga state
//
// Per Comic Ch4 P8 invariant ("One Identity to Rule Them All"): a single
// GCID carries DIFFERENT roles per course. ResolveRoleByCourse returns the
// role context within a specific course; agents (AGID) cannot hold
// TenantMembership (ddd-enforcement aggregate-invariant #10).
//
// Closure saga RPCs (InitiateClosure / AdvanceClosure) are the synchronous
// control-plane entrypoints — actual per-domain pseudonymisation runs
// asynchronously via Pub/Sub events fanned out by the AI-Kernel-owned
// ClosureOrchestrator (see proto/services/closure_orchestrator.proto).
//
// Deployed in chora-local team-platform pool. mTLS via the service mesh;
// SPIFFE identity in mesh; W3C trace context in gRPC metadata.
// =============================================================================

